[[:db/retract 17592186124919 :question/answer-fields 17592186122114] {:db/id 17592186124919 :question/problem "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ with $f(x)=\\frac{3x+4}{6-15x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3x+4}{6-15x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{3x}{x}+\\frac{4}{x})}{(\\frac{6}{x}-\\frac{15x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(3+\\frac{4}{x})}{(\\frac{6}{x}-15)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+0}{0-15} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-\\frac{1}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-381810c0-51a5-5b82-b7b6-6ce8ed23d924"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-381810c0-51a5-5b82-b7b6-6ce8ed23d924" :answer-field/id #uuid "381810c0-51a5-5b82-b7b6-6ce8ed23d924" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-521202c4-e823-5b6e-92ea-799e96ebcde5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9123a10f-7315-5079-b272-8ae329eb3b75" "answer-521202c4-e823-5b6e-92ea-799e96ebcde5" "answer-18f73f57-316e-5fb3-bc4a-e767aaf24db8" "answer-cf5c50b9-a9ea-50a2-a08b-b1461f5b7bb9" "answer-30464325-d158-5e08-93a8-e607ad63b4a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9123a10f-7315-5079-b272-8ae329eb3b75" :answer/id #uuid "9123a10f-7315-5079-b272-8ae329eb3b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-521202c4-e823-5b6e-92ea-799e96ebcde5" :answer/id #uuid "521202c4-e823-5b6e-92ea-799e96ebcde5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18f73f57-316e-5fb3-bc4a-e767aaf24db8" :answer/id #uuid "18f73f57-316e-5fb3-bc4a-e767aaf24db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf5c50b9-a9ea-50a2-a08b-b1461f5b7bb9" :answer/id #uuid "cf5c50b9-a9ea-50a2-a08b-b1461f5b7bb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30464325-d158-5e08-93a8-e607ad63b4a6" :answer/id #uuid "30464325-d158-5e08-93a8-e607ad63b4a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124664 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e2d47372-f9cb-5c02-86fd-148b7f1d18b1" "question-88ec9ee8-0b06-53f7-bc3c-92317b5059e7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2d47372-f9cb-5c02-86fd-148b7f1d18b1" :question/id #uuid "e2d47372-f9cb-5c02-86fd-148b7f1d18b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-101320" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}+1}{{x}^{3}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{4}+1}{{x}^{3}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(x+0)}{(1-0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-36e0c9a9-15c6-51ff-ac4a-304c0aa988be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36e0c9a9-15c6-51ff-ac4a-304c0aa988be" :answer-field/id #uuid "36e0c9a9-15c6-51ff-ac4a-304c0aa988be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cad17541-13af-57a0-9141-29e20640a0ce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db92d19b-e030-57a9-b3fd-2d1169f5e7a8" "answer-0051830d-55e5-5121-b11a-0d87da7f40fb" "answer-0e733fa1-bbd0-5f83-a1a9-64ce04aed72b" "answer-a7b385fb-ca34-55cc-a656-aaa065330917" "answer-cad17541-13af-57a0-9141-29e20640a0ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db92d19b-e030-57a9-b3fd-2d1169f5e7a8" :answer/id #uuid "db92d19b-e030-57a9-b3fd-2d1169f5e7a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0051830d-55e5-5121-b11a-0d87da7f40fb" :answer/id #uuid "0051830d-55e5-5121-b11a-0d87da7f40fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e733fa1-bbd0-5f83-a1a9-64ce04aed72b" :answer/id #uuid "0e733fa1-bbd0-5f83-a1a9-64ce04aed72b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7b385fb-ca34-55cc-a656-aaa065330917" :answer/id #uuid "a7b385fb-ca34-55cc-a656-aaa065330917" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cad17541-13af-57a0-9141-29e20640a0ce" :answer/id #uuid "cad17541-13af-57a0-9141-29e20640a0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-88ec9ee8-0b06-53f7-bc3c-92317b5059e7" :question/id #uuid "88ec9ee8-0b06-53f7-bc3c-92317b5059e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-101322" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{9{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x}{5{x}^{2}+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x}{5{x}^{2}+3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(9x+1-\\frac{1}{x})}{(5+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(9x+1-0)}{(5+0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(9x+1) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e22bffa8-51cb-5c7c-a8dc-24d845160961"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e22bffa8-51cb-5c7c-a8dc-24d845160961" :answer-field/id #uuid "e22bffa8-51cb-5c7c-a8dc-24d845160961" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4ee551d-2ce2-5847-a076-aa2475baa979" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f405f918-ce19-52f9-9c3d-f68c97ea5cd2" "answer-20243682-29c5-5259-864f-3c811fbe7f7d" "answer-95bed720-0647-52ed-9834-06d42bf8de74" "answer-4f14c146-ddb9-57bd-ad6f-3930420ac403" "answer-b4ee551d-2ce2-5847-a076-aa2475baa979"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f405f918-ce19-52f9-9c3d-f68c97ea5cd2" :answer/id #uuid "f405f918-ce19-52f9-9c3d-f68c97ea5cd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20243682-29c5-5259-864f-3c811fbe7f7d" :answer/id #uuid "20243682-29c5-5259-864f-3c811fbe7f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95bed720-0647-52ed-9834-06d42bf8de74" :answer/id #uuid "95bed720-0647-52ed-9834-06d42bf8de74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f14c146-dd